description:
Four assertions in the campaign schedule tests compare a `Duration` against `Duration::ZERO` with `>=`:

```
assert!(shard.timing.draw >= Duration::ZERO);
assert!(shard.timing.pack >= Duration::ZERO);
assert!(shard.timing.evaluate >= Duration::ZERO);
assert!(shard.timing.count >= Duration::ZERO);
```

`Duration` is unsigned, so every one of these holds for any value including zero. They assert nothing, and would keep passing if a phase stopped being measured entirely — which is the exact defect class found in the accelerator path under a39bb161, where `pack` was reported as zero while packing happened.

`@/inv/semantic-test-assertions` requires tests to assert observable semantic properties. A test that cannot fail is not coverage.

## Success Criteria

- [hard] REQ-01: Each of the four assertions either states a property that can fail for a wrong implementation — for example that a phase a backend genuinely performs records a non-zero span, and that a phase it genuinely skips records zero — or is removed as coverage that was never there.

## Notes

Pre-existing in crates/gf2-sim/src/permanent_campaign/schedule.rs; confirmed absent from the a39bb161 diff. Surfaced by the epic-b8206228 execution lead during the a39bb161 phase-attribution review.
